Don't full-repaint a self-painting composited layer that merely moved.

Root cause of the franceinfo.fr scroll slowness (device-proven, build 524):
the page runs a full document layout on ~every scroll frame, and the
post-layout RenderLayer::recursiveUpdateLayerPositions ->
RenderElement::repaintAfterLayoutIfNeeded fully repaints each composited
section layer whose outline-bounds *location* changed (RenderElement.cpp
~L1439: "if our outline bounds rect moved, we have to repaint everything").
franceinfo has ~14 such composited section layers (each 1-2 viewports tall);
each one full-repaints per scroll frame. Measured against onche.org with an
identical scroll (WEBKIT_PAINT_LOG): franceinfo 70 full-layer invalidations /
76.7 Mpx vs onche 14 / 6.6 Mpx = 11.6x, i.e. the felt ~10x slowdown. 38 of 95
layers were seen oscillating +/-1px in height per scroll (subpixel layout
jitter) -> a full-layer repaint each.

For a *self-painting composited layer* (its own coordinated backing store),
a pure move -- or a <=1px size jitter -- does NOT require re-rastering the
whole backing: the compositor repositions the layer (setPosition during the
compositing geometry update) and the tiled backing paints any newly exposed
tiles on demand (exactly the invariant webkit-no-full-repaint-on-layer-grow
already relies on). So skip the redundant whole-layer content repaint.

Guarded tightly to stay correct: only when the full repaint is due to a
move/jitter (both rects non-empty and intersecting, size delta <=1px, no
decoration-size repaint required) and NOT a forced full repaint
(RequiresFullRepaint::Yes, e.g. style-driven), and only for a layer that owns
its backing store (!paintsIntoCompositedAncestor && !paintsIntoWindow) -- a
layer painting into an ancestor still needs the ancestor invalidated at both
positions. WEBKIT_REPAINT_ON_COMPOSITED_MOVE=1 restores stock behaviour (A/B).

--- a/Source/WebCore/rendering/RenderElement.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/rendering/RenderElement.cpp
@@ -74,6 +74,7 @@
 #include "RenderInline.h"
 #include "RenderIterator.h"
 #include "RenderLayer.h"
+#include "RenderLayerBacking.h"
 #include "RenderLayerCompositor.h"
 #include "RenderLayerInlines.h"
 #include "RenderLayerScrollableArea.h"
@@ -109,6 +110,7 @@
 #include "Styleable.h"
 #include "TextAutoSizing.h"
 #include "ViewTransition.h"
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <wtf/MathExtras.h>
 #include <wtf/StackStats.h>
 #include <wtf/TZoneMallocInlines.h>
@@ -1450,6 +1452,41 @@
     if (!repaintContainer)
         repaintContainer = &view();
 
+#if USE(COORDINATED_GRAPHICS)
+    // A self-painting composited layer that merely moved during layout (or
+    // jittered <=1px in size) does not need its whole backing store re-rastered:
+    // the compositor repositions the layer and the coordinated tiled backing
+    // paints newly exposed tiles on demand (same invariant as
+    // webkit-no-full-repaint-on-layer-grow). franceinfo.fr relayouts on ~every
+    // scroll frame, so without this each of ~14 composited section layers
+    // full-repaints per frame (device-proven: ~11x onche.org's full-layer paint
+    // = the felt ~10x scroll slowdown). WEBKIT_REPAINT_ON_COMPOSITED_MOVE=1
+    // restores stock behaviour.
+    if (fullRepaint && requiresFullRepaint != RequiresFullRepaint::Yes && haveOutlinesBoundsRects
+        && !oldClippedOverflowRect.isEmpty() && !newClippedOverflowRect.isEmpty()
+        && oldClippedOverflowRect.intersects(newClippedOverflowRect)) {
+        auto widthDelta = newRects.outlineBoundsRect->width() - oldRects.outlineBoundsRect->width();
+        auto heightDelta = newRects.outlineBoundsRect->height() - oldRects.outlineBoundsRect->height();
+        if (widthDelta < 0)
+            widthDelta = -widthDelta;
+        if (heightDelta < 0)
+            heightDelta = -heightDelta;
+        static bool repaintOnCompositedMove = [] {
+            const char* v = getenv("WEBKIT_REPAINT_ON_COMPOSITED_MOVE");
+            return v && *v && *v != '0';
+        }();
+        if (!repaintOnCompositedMove && widthDelta <= LayoutUnit(1) && heightDelta <= LayoutUnit(1)
+            && !mustRepaintBackgroundOrBorderOnSizeChange(*oldRects.outlineBoundsRect, *newRects.outlineBoundsRect)) {
+            if (auto* layerModelObject = dynamicDowncast<RenderLayerModelObject>(*this)) {
+                if (auto* layer = layerModelObject->layer(); layer && layer->isComposited()) {
+                    if (auto* backing = layer->backing(); backing && !backing->paintsIntoCompositedAncestor() && !backing->paintsIntoWindow())
+                        return true; // compositor moves the backing; skip the redundant full content repaint
+                }
+            }
+        }
+    }
+#endif
+
     if (fullRepaint) {
         if (newClippedOverflowRect.contains(oldClippedOverflowRect))
             repaintUsingContainer(WeakPtr { repaintContainer }, newClippedOverflowRect);
